# Vendored upstream trees are stored BYTE-IDENTICAL to their pinned commit, so that
# `diff -ru <pristine-clone> vendor/<x>` recovers exactly our patch list and nothing
# else. Git's automatic CRLF normalisation would silently rewrite upstream files that
# ship with CRLF (Carcasum vendors quazip, whose MSVC project files do), turning a
# clean diff into dozens of phantom whole-file changes and breaking the
# "minimal and re-appliable" contract in vendor/carcasum/CARCASUM_PATCHES.md.
vendor/** -text

# Same reasoning for the checked-in reference XML the tile oracles pin by sha256:
# tests/test_jcz_tile_oracle.py and tests/test_carcasum_tile_oracle.py assert the
# vendored bytes, so any normalisation would fail those tests rather than pass
# quietly -- but pinning here means the failure never happens in the first place.
tests/data/jcz/*.xml -text
tests/data/carcasum/*.xml -text
